      "problem": "If $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}+x-6,$ then ${A}^{3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's divide the polynomial $f(x)={x}^{3}$ by characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}+x-6,$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"left\">$\\,\\,x$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$-$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">${x}^{2}+x-6\\,$</td>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"left\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{3}\\phantom{|}\\,\\,}$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">${x}^{3}$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$+$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">${x}^{2}$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$-$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$6x$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$-$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">${x}^{2}$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$+$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$6x$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$-$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">${x}^{2}$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$-$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$+$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$7x$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$-$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"20\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write ${x}^{3}$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =q(x)p(x)+(7x-6),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)=x-1.$  Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{3}=q(A)p(A)+(7A-6I).\n$$\n\nNow, according to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3} & =q(A)p(A)+(7A-6I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(7A-6I) \\\\  & =7A-6I.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
